{
  "$comment": "Wording for the reference form (Finland, in plain Finnish, addressing the reader as 'sinä', as Finnish public services do). Change wording, hints and error messages here, not in code. Field rules live in ../enquiry-submission.schema.json. Optional questions end with '(vapaaehtoinen)', which the Suomi.fi components show in the regular weight; required ones carry no mark. The location question asks only for the first 3 digits of the postcode (postinumero): enough to find the wellbeing services county (hyvinvointialue) that recruits foster families, or the City of Helsinki, which runs its own services. A full postcode is cut to its first 3 digits. 'team' and 'kinship_team' are in the elative case (-sta, -stä), because they follow a name: 'Aino perhehoidon tiimistä'. Not yet checked by a native speaker.",
  "locale": "fi-FI",
  "design_system": "suomifi",
